#: data/com.excelano.Comma.desktop.in:2
#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:5 src/gtk/window.blp:5
#: src/gtk/window.blp:17
msgid "Comma"
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.desktop.in:3
#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:6
msgid "Edit delimited text files"
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.desktop.in:10
msgid "CSV;TSV;DSV;Delimited;Table;Data;"
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:12
msgid ""
"Comma is a small editor for CSV, TSV, and other delimited text files. It "
"shows a file as a grid of values and saves it back as the same kind of file "
"it opened, leaving every row you did not edit byte for byte as it was."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:18
msgid ""
"Values are treated as text and never reinterpreted, so leading zeros "
"survive, long identifiers stay whole, and dates are whatever the file says "
"they are."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:23
msgid ""
"Comma is not a spreadsheet. There are no formulas, no cell formatting, and "
"no second file format to save into."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:32
msgid "David M. Anderson"
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:44
msgid ""
"The last column can be made wider or narrower like every other one. Its "
"right edge answers to a drag from either side of the line, where before it "
"was the one edge in the table that answered to nothing."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:49
msgid ""
"Resizing a column no longer moves the keyboard. Taking hold of a column used "
"to put the cursor on a cell, and the cursor is what decides which row or "
"column the next insert or delete happens to. It now stays where you left it."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:59
msgid ""
"The files you have had open are a click away. The arrow beside Open lists "
"them, newest first, with a box to search through them when the list is long. "
"Clicking one opens it here, and asks first if there is anything unsaved in "
"the window."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:65
msgid ""
"Comma also puts the files it opens into the desktop's own recent documents "
"now, so a file edited here turns up in the Files sidebar and wherever else "
"your desktop lists what you have been working on. Saving under a new name "
"files that name as well."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:71
msgid ""
"A file opened from a share or a server says which folder it is in, where "
"before it said nothing."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:79
msgid ""
"Comma can open a second window. A button at the left of the header bar, or "
"Ctrl+N, gives you an empty one to open another file in, which until now took "
"naming both files on the command line or quitting Comma first. Ctrl+W closes "
"the window you are in, and asks before it goes if there is anything unsaved "
"in it."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:86
msgid ""
"Saving a file under another name, and writing one out as a PDF, a web page "
"or a spreadsheet, have moved out of the main menu to the arrow beside the "
"Save button, a click from the button they belong to."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:92
msgid "The exports no longer offer themselves on a window with no file open."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:100
msgid ""
"Comma now guesses whether the first row of a file is column titles or data, "
"the way it already guessed the delimiter. A column of figures with a word "
"over it has a title on it; a column that runs figures all the way to the top "
"does not."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:106
msgid ""
"Both guesses sit under the header bar button that says how the file is being "
"read, and both are one click from being corrected. Correcting this one "
"settles it: changing the delimiter afterwards makes the guess again only "
"while it is still a guess, and never overrules an answer you gave."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:117
msgid ""
"Comma can now hand the file, or the folder it sits in, to something else. "
"The primary menu opens the containing folder, or a terminal already standing "
"in it, so there is no path to retype."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:122
msgid ""
"It can also open the file in xled, xql or nved, each offered only when it is "
"installed. Comma tells them what it has already worked out about the file — "
"which delimiter it is reading and whether the first row is a header — so the "
"tool comes up on the same view of the file rather than working it out again."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:129
msgid ""
"A file with unsaved edits offers to save before it is handed over, since the "
"tool reads what is on disk."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:137
msgid ""
"Comma now notices when something else writes the file it has open. If "
"nothing is unsaved it reads the file again and says so; if there are edits "
"to lose, or a cell is open for typing, it says the file has changed and "
"waits to be asked."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:143
msgid ""
"Saving over a file that has been written to since Comma read it now asks "
"first, and offers to save this version somewhere else instead."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:147
msgid ""
"Reading the file again keeps the sorting, the column conditions, how far "
"across the file you had scrolled and the row you were on."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:155
msgid ""
"Fixes a fault that could make Comma stop responding after a cell had been "
"opened for typing. Every version before this one is affected, so this is "
"worth updating to."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:164
msgid ""
"Clicking a row number now moves the keyboard there even in the moment after "
"a filter or a search has changed what is showing, rather than quietly doing "
"nothing."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:169
msgid ""
"Tabbing through the window goes from the toolbar straight into the table. It "
"used to stop at the row numbers, which answer to the mouse and had no key to "
"press."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:178
msgid ""
"Any column can be held to a condition of its own. Right-click its heading "
"and pick from nine: contains and does not contain, is and is not, is empty "
"and is not empty, is greater than, is less than, and is between. Several "
"columns can each carry one, and they narrow one another."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:185
msgid ""
"Right-clicking a cell offers the shortest way in — hold this column to the "
"value already written here. Numbers are read as numbers, so a price above "
"100 turns up neither a blank cell nor one priced in sterling."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:191
msgid ""
"Every condition in force is spelled out on a bar under the toolbar with the "
"button that removes it, and the title now says how many rows of how many are "
"showing, whether a filter or a search is what left them out."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:201
msgid ""
"Wide files draw faster. A file of forty-odd columns took about a second to "
"put its table on the screen and now takes around half of that, because the "
"height of a line of text is measured once for the whole grid rather than "
"again for every cell in it."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:207
msgid ""
"Building Comma from source now gives you an optimised binary. Asking Meson "
"for one had quietly been giving you the opposite."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:215
msgid ""
"The row numbers stay put when the grid is scrolled sideways, as the column "
"headings already did, so the number naming a row is beside it however far "
"across a wide file you have gone."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:220
msgid ""
"A row inserted mid-file no longer misnumbers the rows below it, and an edit "
"made to one of those rows is written to the row you typed into rather than "
"to the one above it."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:229
msgid ""
"Files open quickly. A cell now builds its editor when you type in it rather "
"than when the grid is drawn, so a file of four thousand rows opens in a "
"moment rather than in a couple of seconds, and a wide file gains the most."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:235
msgid ""
"Inserting or deleting a row redraws that row rather than the whole grid, so "
"the table stays where you had scrolled it to."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:243
msgid ""
"The first release. Comma opens a delimited file, guesses its delimiter and "
"says which one it guessed, and edits it as a grid. Rows and columns can be "
"inserted and deleted, everything can be undone, and saving a file changes "
"only the lines you edited."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:249
msgid ""
"Sorting and searching are views of the file rather than changes to it, and "
"one menu item writes a sort order down when you want it. What the grid is "
"showing can be exported as a PDF, a web page, or an OpenDocument spreadsheet."
msgstr ""

